WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:12.500
Located in the Persian Gulf, Qatar is a country
with an area of little more than 10,000 square

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.310
kilometers. Just to give you some idea of
just how small that it, it is nearly 40 times

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.960
smaller than California.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:25.130
So, when this country got its independence
from the UK in 1971, Qatar was faraway, hostile

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.770
and and very poor place.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:31.750
As a matter of fact, it was one of the poorest
territories of the United Kingdom.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.360
And that made a lot of sense…

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.270
The Qatar Peninsula is a place where temperatures
can reach 50º Celsius in summer, it is almost

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.030
completely covered by desert and it was certainly
one of the most uninhabitable places on Earth.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:49.341
But it didn’t stay that way forever and
today Qatar is the richest country on the

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:50.341
planet.

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:57.829
That´s right, the citizens of this tiny country
enjoy a per capita income of more than $125,000,

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:09.070
which is almost three times the income in
France and five times that found in Chile...

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.960
This is a country which was almost uninhabited,
a country that could hardly survive on its

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:21.999
fishing industry, and today it looks something
like Scrooge McDuck’s safe.

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:27.959
The government of Qatar has investments and
properties all around the world. It is the

00:01:27.959 --> 00:01:33.350
birthplace of Al Jazeera, the most important
Arabic media company and then there is Doha,

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:38.529
the capital, which is a sea of skyscrapers,
malls and luxurious cars.

00:01:38.529 --> 00:01:42.770
“A mix of Monaco and Vegas, but without
the alcohol and gambling. There is no room

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:48.171
for simplicity, everything is sumptuous, hugh
and sparkling in Doha”. Ángel Sastre, Conflict

00:01:48.171 --> 00:01:49.380
areas reporter.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.420
Qatar has gone from being a dark shelter for
wahhabist preachers and has become what might

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.349
people might consider the most open country
in the middle east. (Other than Dubai, of

00:01:58.349 --> 00:02:02.539
course, but as you might know Dubai is an
emirate and not actually a country).

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:10.790
In modern day Doha, we can find international
universities or the so-called “Church City”:

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:17.319
a complex of protestant, orthodox and Catholic
churches… like the Church of Our Lady of

00:02:17.319 --> 00:02:18.319
Rosary.

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:23.849
“The $20m Catholic church, which seats 2,700,
is located in the southern outskirts of the

00:02:23.849 --> 00:02:28.599
city on land donated by Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa
al-Thani, Qatar's emir”.

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:33.800
So, now the question of course has to be:
How did Qatar achieve this remarkable transformation?

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.790
Well, let’s take a look at that.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:41.860
THE LNG BLESSING: LIQUIFIED NATURAL GAS

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:46.920
In other videos we have discussed some of
the keys why some countries are so rich. But

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.989
in Qatar´s case it is much simpler and it
can be summarized by two things:

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:58.390
Oil and, more importantly, natural gas…
a massive amount of natural gas.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.790
Yep, that is pretty much it…

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.670
Disappointed? Well, hold on a second because
it is actually quite an interesting story...

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:12.120
The first oil fields were found in the 1940s,
and by the 1960s exploitation was already

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:18.290
consolidated. And things in the poor country
of Qatar changed… but not a huge amount.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.969
The thing is that it wasn’t until the beginning
of the 1970s that Shell found the biggest

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.939
treasure of this country:

00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:30.469
“The North Field”, the largest gas field
in the world.

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:37.189
But… at that time natural gas was not really
that profitable.

00:03:37.189 --> 00:03:41.601
You see, at that time, gas could only be transported
through gas pipes and Qatar was far too far

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:46.730
away from anywhere where the gas could be
used. Even Shell soon forgot about &nbsp;it...

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:50.099
But, well, things they were about to change.

00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:56.310
In 1996, the old emir, Hamad bin Khalifa al-Thani
(who abdicated in 2013) staged a coup d'etat

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:01.870
while his father was in Switzerland. This
emir reached power with a very clear idea:

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:07.269
the future of Qatar was gas, they had to exploit
their huge fields.

00:04:07.269 --> 00:04:08.859
And so he did.

00:04:08.859 --> 00:04:13.329
The new emir decided to invest in an undeveloped
and rare technology:

00:04:13.329 --> 00:04:18.139
Liquefaction, which is the ability to carry
natural gas in a liquid form so it could be

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:21.190
transported in large ships as if it were oil.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.340
In order to do this, the gas needs to cool
down and be kept at a temperature of -161º

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:39.820
Celsius (-258 F). Which is just a touch inconvenient…
So Qatar decided to invest enormous quantities

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:45.210
of resources to boost the development of this
technology so it could be used on a massive

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.210
scale.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:50.410
Because of that investment Qatar is now the
world’s largest exporter of LNG. With this

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:54.650
technology, Qatar is able to export its enormous
gas supplies to the rest of the world.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:59.430
In fact, last year, three quarters of Qatar's
gas went to Asian countries like China, India,

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.660
South Korea and Japan.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:05.680
And there is more: the industrial complex
Qatar has developed is so big, so large-scale,

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:11.270
that the country has managed to have the cheapest
costs of extraction and liquefaction in the

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:12.590
world.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:17.660
To illustrate this, a methane tanker of LNG
is four times cheaper in Qatar than it is

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.280
in the United States!

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.350
And this, dear viewer, is the big secret of
this small and wealthy country.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:29.220
Now, this is only a part of the equation.
Not only does a country need to exploit the

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:34.570
resources, but they also need to use the money
it generates well, or they are going to end

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.900
up like Angola or Venezuela...

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:45.120
So besides this innovative process, Qatar
has some other keys to their success.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.780
QATAR’S POWER

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:56.010
Since Hamad bin Khalifa al-Thani reached power
in 1995, things have changed significantly.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:06:01.440
In his 18 years leading the country, Qatar´s
population has multiplied by 5, while at the

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.090
same time becoming richest country on Earth.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:11.560
So, the old emir has plenty of reasons to
feel proud of himself.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:16.940
But, let’s move on... Qatar started to generate
a lot of economic resources and, well, what

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:19.460
do you think they are doing with this money?

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:24.150
Well, despite what it may look like, they
have mainly invested it (both nationally and

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:30.970
internationally). Qatar has created the “Qatar
Investment Authority”, a huge fund to invest

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.740
money all around the world.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:37.610
It is known as “Qatar’s Power” because
they can have in their hands, more than $330

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:39.140
billion!!

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:44.580
And hey, the population of Qatar is less than
3 million, but of these 3 million people…

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:49.300
only 300,000 are Qatari citizens, so, well,
you can do the math.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:56.970
This fund has made significant real estate
investments all over the world…

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:01.840
In London, a big part of the city belongs
to Qatar, including hotels, offices, apartments…and

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:07.430
in the United States, Qatar was, in 2016,
the fourth largest office investor in the

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:12.710
country. In Manhattan alone, this fund has
invested $5 billion in the last two years.

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:18.680
And it is not just real estate, this fund
also has major shares in many multinationals:

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:22.750
Qatar is, for instance, one of the largest
shareholder of companies like Volkswagen,

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:28.340
Iberdrola, Barclays Bank, Tiffany &amp; co, Shell
or even the giant Rosneft, the oil company

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.710
of the Russian government.

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:33.330
In the image we are about to show you can
see how foreign investment has increased as

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:41.430
the production of gas and oil has grown:
And it’s not just international investment

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:45.300
- they are also investing lots of resources
inside the country:

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:50.470
Tens of billions has been spent on highways,
ports, airports, research centres, financial

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:53.300
centres… and so on.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:57.800
And, well, what’s the goal of all of this?
Well, that’s to be able to, in the future,

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:02.860
replace with the income they get from oil
and gas, with the income from these investments...

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:08.410
But the moment when the gas business runs
out is still too far away to really be a problem.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:13.240
"There are no analysts who can say when demand
for gas will wane. For oil, there are people

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:19.360
who see peak demand in 2030, others in 2042,
but for gas, demand is constantly growing."

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.120
This idea they have in investing, instead
of spending the money, from natural resources

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:28.501
might be one of the most important differences
between Qatar and other countries who are

00:08:28.501 --> 00:08:29.840
also rich in natural resources.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:34.760
Most of them find it too easy to spend the
money today, and not think too much about

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:41.810
the future...
TOWARDS EFFECTIVE INDEPENDENCE

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:49.190
When Hamad bin Khalifa al-Thani reached power,
he also had another thing in mind: Qatar had

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:50.830
to gain international influence.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:56.000
You see, for years, Qatar was controlled,
de facto, by Saudi Arabia and the new emir

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.670
just couldn’t forget about Iraq’s invasion
of Kuwait.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:04.400
If Qatar wanted to survive they needed to
claim their identity and gain international

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:10.210
influence. Otherwise, any conflict with Riyadh
could compromise the independence of the country.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:21.230
Besides, natural gas could pay the bills now...
So, in 2003, when Saudi Arabia “requested”

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:26.370
that the US take American troops out of their
country, Qatar didn’t hesitate to offer

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:31.900
itself as a destination for those troops.
They didn’t even blink when it came to spending

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.430
about a billion dollars to build the military
bases...

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:44.820
“The sprawling base 20 miles southwest of
the Qatari capital of Doha is home to some

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:48.920
11,000 US military personnel”.
Indeed, it could be said that Qatar has taken

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:52.400
out a very comprehensive insurance policy…

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:57.180
And then we have the founding of Al Jazeera.
This has the objective of obtaining global

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:03.640
influence, and they succeeded - something
we actually covered in a previous video!

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:11.990
They also developed a foreign policy driving
towards international influence.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:13.710
THE BLOCKADE

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:19.279
All this political strategy made both the
United Arab Emirates and Saudi Arabia very

00:10:19.279 --> 00:10:25.340
angry. In June of 2017, they announced a blockade,
accusing Qatar of supporting fundamentalist

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:31.170
groups and terrorists.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:33.620
Pot calling the kettle black Saudi Arabia?
Hmmm?

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:38.241
Now, it is true Qatar has some dark secrets,
it is an absolute monarchy after all… But

00:10:38.241 --> 00:10:43.990
the country is a good ally for the West, especially
the US, and it is one of the most open countries

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:44.990
in the region.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:50.140
The truth is the boycott had a different target:
to cut down Qatar’s strategy of international

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:53.330
influence and to essentially put them in their
place…

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:56.800
However, the blockade has been a total failure...

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.660
First, Riyadh’s position is not that strong...
Very few countries have supported it, not

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.440
even Kuwait or Oman.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:07.690
Also, Qatar has developed better relationships
with Turkey and even Iran... Qatar has simply

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:09.830
proved they are strong enough to weather the
storm.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:12.060
“Qatar defies Saudi Arabia by restoring
diplomatic ties with Iran”.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.770
And finally, something does need to be made
clear:

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:18.370
There are plenty of grey areas in Qatar: labour
conditions that are more consistent with the

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:23.680
ones of a poor country, the situation of women,
and the lack of democracy.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:27.319
Furthermore, the system needs to prove it
can work without the government, because,

00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:31.940
unlike Dubai, the lead has been taken by public
initiative, not private.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:36.700
And this is one of the reasons why Dubai is
still above Qatar in pretty much all aspects.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:41.310
But, hey, it wouldn’t be fair to acknowledge
what they are doing right, like their saving

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:46.990
capacity, their productive investment, and
their openness.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:52.210
And now is your turn, who do you think will
win this battle of the countries in the Persian

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:55.440
Gulf? Saudi Arabia or will it be Qatar?

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:59.230
Leave your answer in the comments below, as
well as in this survey.

